※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5005 LANG_STMT_VALUE_DISCARDED
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5006 LANG_STMT_ASSIGNMENT_IS_AN_ARROW

※ A comparison is one of the expressions whose value must be used, like every
※ other, and the one that gets a note of its own: written with '=' it is what
※ someone produces who has spent years in a language where '=' assigns.  The
※ last statement of a body is the body's result, so the second one here is the
※ point of the function and only the first is reported.
let a: u8 = 1u8
let b: u8 = 2u8

@[startup]
fn main() → bool:
    a = b
    a > b
